{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12917-if-we-got-a-book-introducing-new-courts-what-would-you-want","id":12917,"title":"If we got a book introducing New Courts what would you want?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-17T13:31:38-08:00","id":12917,"title":"If we got a book introducing New Courts what would you want?","content":"Say we got a book introducing New Courts to the game, what would you want? Personally I'm hungry for any new changeling material, and I find Court systems to be well quite fun, and not only that but as far as optional alternative systems go they are among the best and most usable in the NWOD!<br /> <br /> So what Court Systems would you like to see?<br /> <br /> I would like it if they put in the missing courts that go with Dawn and Dusk, or possibly an explanation for connecting them to the Sun and Moon courts (perhaps sun and moon fit the roles of Day and Night when combined with the Dusk and Dawn Courts.).<br /> <br /> <br /> The Books also mention a Buddhist Cycle Court, and an African Predator Prey Foodchain Court. If someone came up with a good pitch for these I wouldn't mind seeing them, but I also wouldn't mind ignoring them as they haven't been introduced as incomplete like the other courts.<br /> <br /> <br /> What Court Emotions/Contracts do think would be fun to have? Once Again I wish they finished the ones for the Sun and Moon Court because we already have these courts in the books but they are damned incomplete!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T13:42:05-08:00","id":12927,"title":"","content":"I think an Ashrama Court based on the Hindu Four Stages of Life would be interesting. Such as <br /> <br /> <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brahmacharya\" target=\"_blank\">Brahmacharya</a></i><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">(student life) </span></span></div><br /> <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grihastha\" target=\"_blank\">Grihastha</a></i><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">(household life)</span></span></div><br /> <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanaprastha\" target=\"_blank\">Vanaprastha</a></i><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">(retired life)</span></span></div><br /> <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sannyasa\" target=\"_blank\">Sannyasa</a></i><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">(renounced life)<br /> <br /> <br /> This would be interesting in how they handled court rule. Perhaps each stage would have one who rules all members of the Freehold of their court, so like the Directional Courts they are not divided by seasons but by membership or age/maturity? Or they could run on the Seasonal Cycle with Brahmacharya starting in Spring, and Sannyasa in Winter. Perhaps the period of the Sannyasa rule is a hands off time where folks are not constrained by Courtly politics? I can't help but feel a number of cool contracts could be spawned from this idea. Particularly Contracts for the Sannyasa.<br /> <br /> <br /> This could be say mirrored with a western Norn/Moirae Court of the Maiden Mother Crone Courts. Or perhaps the men of a Freehold take up the Ashrama Court and the Women take up the Norn/Moirae Courts.</span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:16:54-08:00","id":12950,"title":"","content":"Glamourweaver has a concept for the Arabian Court of Days that I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> I'd very much like a bit of polish on the Moon Court; change it's emotion to Joy and a bit more emphasis on &quot;not really evil&quot; to balance the Sun's &quot;not really good&quot; and both courts knowingly relying on each other to stop them going too far.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd also quite like a Court system specifically for games that focus mostly interaction with the human world. Let's call it the Courts of Flowers. Flowers are cool and pretty.<br /> <br /> One court that's all about family, they want their old family or to start a new one. They are stereotyped as clingy. Emotion: Dependency. <br /> <br /> One court that's all about being accepted for who they are. That means refusing to fix their Changeling related mental issues. Emotion: Stubbornness.<br /> <br /> One court that's about being useful to people while avoiding notice, based on myths of household brownies and similar. Emotion: Contentment.<br /> <br /> One court that's about gaining fame and/or fortune in the human world. Emotion: Ambition.<br /> <br /> 1 and 2 are polar opposites: Change everything about yourself to please a boy/girlfriend vs change nothing. 3 and 4 are also opposites: Humility vs loudness.<br /> <br /> <br /> No flower court has a king, instead the Wyrd crowns one mortal to rule over the freehold. This mortal is chosen as the person who is most able to:<br /> 1) Know what the other mortals in the Freehold's area would want the Freehold to do; if they knew it existed.<br /> 2) Know how to get the highly dysfunctional (seriously, these guys look worse than the Directional Courts) Freehold to do that.<br /> <br /> The Crown would grant the ability to see faeries, the ability to travel the hedge, and a really good defence - say reduce all successes by 5 - against magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> It just needs four symbolically appropriate flowers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:24:01-08:00","id":12961,"title":"","content":"Wow that sounds cool, and the Crown choosing the mortal is a brilliantly unique idea! I like having a court that fits Brownies and Domovoi. Too bad I suck at Flower Symbolism. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T15:24:31-08:00","id":12998,"title":"","content":"While I love the game, I'd certainly like to see a more modern kind of thing. Where I grew up we didn't really have autumn, and winter was like a couple of weeks where things got into the freezing 70s. As an aside, there's also no basements or sewers that can fit a people walking in them, so those being a sort of universal across WoD bug me.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I honestly have no idea how they'd do it. Twitter/reddit/Youtube/4chan? No clue!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T15:32:17-08:00","id":13001,"title":"","content":"Basements and Sewers? Are you referring to the Hedge?<br /> <br /> Hey that's a actually an interesting gem, what about a modern technology based Court System. So Internet, TV, Transit, Infrastructure based Court?! This would be perfect for a Godmachine game!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh now that got me thinking, what about a Sky, Sea, and Land Court System? That would be interesting and simple, and I would love the Court Contracts associated with it. I wonder how much you can play with how Courts work, I guess at minimum you need 2, and we already can have that with the Sun and Moon Court. But on the opposite end of the Spectrum I wonder how many Courts you can have in one System?<br /> <br /> What about Weird Courts like a Continent Based Court System?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T16:14:35-08:00","id":13031,"title":"","content":"The basements and sewers was more for world of darkness or horror in general, I suppose vampire more than other splats, vampires are notorious for cellars and sewers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T20:30:27-08:00","id":13148,"title":"","content":"I definitely want to see the hinted at Asian courts too. Actually, a Shinto and Buddhist one inspired by Japan especially could be fun, they've got a pretty grand tradition of &quot;Fae Abductions&quot; too via Kamikakushi (Spirited Away - yes the movie has this in its Japanese Title too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). So there is a lot to draw on there.<br /> <br /> The Arabian one would be marvelous too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T02:14:03-08:00","id":13285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12917-if-we-got-a-book-introducing-new-courts-what-would-you-want?p=12998#post12998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, there's also no basements or sewers that can fit a people walking in them, so those being a sort of universal across WoD bug me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what you're talking about here, but come to England sometime, we have tours of sewers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T23:54:05-08:00","id":18227,"title":"","content":"Wow really Sewer tours? That even Rhymes so you know it must be cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T08:26:24-08:00","id":18419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12917-if-we-got-a-book-introducing-new-courts-what-would-you-want?p=12950#post12950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also quite like a Court system specifically for games that focus mostly interaction with the human world. Let's call it the Courts of Flowers. Flowers are cool and pretty.<br /> <br /> One court that's all about family, they want their old family or to start a new one. They are stereotyped as clingy. Emotion: Dependency.<br /> <br /> One court that's all about being accepted for who they are. That means refusing to fix their Changeling related mental issues. Emotion: Stubbornness.<br /> <br /> One court that's about being useful to people while avoiding notice, based on myths of household brownies and similar. Emotion: Contentment.<br /> <br /> One court that's about gaining fame and/or fortune in the human world. Emotion: Ambition.<br /> <br /> 1 and 2 are polar opposites: Change everything about yourself to please a boy/girlfriend vs change nothing. 3 and 4 are also opposites: Humility vs loudness.<br /> <br /> <br /> No flower court has a king, instead the Wyrd crowns one mortal to rule over the freehold. This mortal is chosen as the person who is most able to:<br /> 1) Know what the other mortals in the Freehold's area would want the Freehold to do; if they knew it existed.<br /> 2) Know how to get the highly dysfunctional (seriously, these guys look worse than the Directional Courts) Freehold to do that.<br /> <br /> The Crown would grant the ability to see faeries, the ability to travel the hedge, and a really good defence - say reduce all successes by 5 - against magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> It just needs four symbolically appropriate flowers</div> </div> </div> </div>1 - Rose (love, passion)<br /> <br /> 2 - Lavender (distrust, devotion)<br /> <br /> 3 - Violet (loyalty, faithfulness)<br /> <br /> 4 - Marigold (desire for riches)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T08:53:47-08:00","id":18433,"title":"","content":"Honestly? I'd rather just see a book that expanded our the Courts we already have in a way that provided additional depth. I want to see detailed write ups of the competing Factions of the Summer Court, the Autumn Court, etc, each with their own practices, traditions, methods and maybe tokens/pledges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img835/1264/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Do you see over yonder, friend Sancho, thirty or forty hulking giants? I intend to do battle with them and slay them.&quot;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/441-nighttrace","name":"NightTrace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar441_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T08:58:56-08:00","id":18436,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I see I'm not the only one who's been thinking up flowers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I actually brainstormed this a while back here's the list I came up with.<br /> <br /> 1- I actually went for honeysuckle as it's a vine which grows on other plants and can choke them. It symbolises The Bond of Love<br /> <br /> 2 - Euphorbia for resolve, the closest I could get to stubbornness. I'm not too keen on this one though, the name just doesn't fit with the others.<br /> <br /> 3 - I went for Violets too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> loyalty, faithfulness and if you look at violets in their shrubs they look kinda humble.<br /> <br /> 4 - Hollyhock. It symbolises pride and ambition which I think fits a little better, it's fame or fortune.<br /> <br /> 5 - The Crown is white lilies: Virginity, Purity, Majesty, It's Heavenly to be with You, Youth. Perfect symbolism.<br /> <br /> <br /> That also gives each court it's own colour which I think is quite fitting: Pink/yellow/bluet/red (hollyhock comes in many colours)/white. I'd hoped to go for a set of spring blooming flowers to riff of their Spring Court but that I gave up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T09:26:30-08:00","id":18455,"title":"","content":"I was trying to find one that were not only symbolically relevant, but had a strongly associated color (red, purple, blue, yellow) and were polarized some how on the color scale (red + purple on the bookends, yellow and blue on each side of the middle, green).<br /> <br /> Over-thinking it, probably. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I had no brilliant ideas for the crown. White Lilies sounds perfect, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T09:36:30-08:00","id":18467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12917-if-we-got-a-book-introducing-new-courts-what-would-you-want?p=18455#post18455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over-thinking it, probably. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing as overthinking it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> seriously though, I spent days trying to get this right and I'm still not completely satisfied. The word Euphorbia just dosn't fit. I didn't come up with the idea of the colour scale or the importance of the colour being commonly known like you did but I did try to tie it into Spring to fit the seasonal courts. I just couldn't find enough spring flowering plants.<br /> <br /> Having a strong colour for each court is a very good idea and one we seem to have both hit on, just IMO, purple and blue are too similar. (Though Lavender's real problem is that distrust and devotion don't fit too well. It's about stubbornness and insisting others do things your way. Basically the Court of Sheldon Cooper)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-26-2013, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T11:19:00-08:00","id":18521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12917-if-we-got-a-book-introducing-new-courts-what-would-you-want?p=18467#post18467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no such thing as overthinking it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> seriously though, I spent days trying to get this right and I'm still not completely satisfied. The word Euphorbia just dosn't fit. I didn't come up with the idea of the colour scale or the importance of the colour being commonly known like you did but I did try to tie it into Spring to fit the seasonal courts. I just couldn't find enough spring flowering plants.<br /> <br /> Having a strong colour for each court is a very good idea and one we seem to have both hit on, just IMO, purple and blue are too similar. (Though Lavender's real problem is that distrust and devotion don't fit too well. It's about stubbornness and insisting others do things your way. Basically the Court of Sheldon Cooper)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Purple &amp; Blue were too close for me, too, but it was a first shot at it. I was also thinking &quot;devotion + distrust = devoted to only one POV, self!&quot;, but that was a stretch, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T12:16:00-08:00","id":18611,"title":"","content":"Do let me know if you get a better idea though. As I said, Euphorbia is a terrible name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T12:26:36-08:00","id":18619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12917-if-we-got-a-book-introducing-new-courts-what-would-you-want?p=18611#post18611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do let me know if you get a better idea though. As I said, Euphorbia is a terrible name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't there some of these that are cactus like? The Cactus Court? The Desert Rose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 11-26-2013, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T12:44:45-08:00","id":18634,"title":"","content":"Lol, but again nope. Cactus has such a strong association with, well the non-flower part of the cactus plant. Plus I kind of want these flowers to all come from a similar part of the world since presumably the founders lived somewhere and chose flowers they knew aobut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"ra