crown just referring to the human individual that gets the crown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T14:58:01-08:00","id":18740,"title":"","content":"The Crown refers to one human individual. BTW, here's the full titles for the Courts I have:<br /> <br /> The Court of Balsam<br /> The Unyielding Flora, The Red Blossom, The Court of Stubbornness.<br /> <br /> The Court of Hollyhock<br /> The Proud Bloom, The Gold Blossom, The Court of Ambition.<br /> <br /> The Court of Honeysuckle<br /> The Choking Vine, The Pink Blossom, The Court of Dependency.<br /> <br /> The Court of Violet<br /> The Humble Herb, The Blue Blossom, The Court of Satisfaction.<br /> <br /> The Lily Crown<br /> The Royal Flower, The White Blossom, The Crown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T15:22:38-08:00","id":18759,"title":"","content":"I think you got something there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T19:40:41-08:00","id":19503,"title":"","content":"I would really LOVE some solid ideas for the African courts--they may well be the oldest courts on earth, unless the Sun and Moon courts are primordial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T18:47:00-08:00","id":20458,"title":"","content":"I could see a court system based on tropical seasons: A Court of Rain promoting abundance and exuberance, and a Court of Drought promoting austerity and restraint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T02:07:55-08:00","id":20555,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about this earlier, but I gave up on it because I thought there were too many options for Weather (Though I wasn't thinking only tropical).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T06:22:09-08:00","id":21139,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested to see a Court that's based around historical reenactments. Essentially, it's a whole lot of cosplay for each of the competing Entitlements. Different factions, different periods of history from different parts of the world. Going beyond the cosplay element, though, you would have three main branches: 1. One devoted to the scholarship and philosophy of the day; 2. One devoted to the warfare of the day; 3. One devoted to the social etiquette of the day.<br /> <br /> The more I think this over, the more it feels like one larger Entitlement, with a number of &quot;sub-Entitlements&quot; underneath it, taking to heart that if you don't know the past, you're doomed to repeat it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1386-thompry","name":"thompry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1386_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T14:57:46-08:00","id":21310,"title":"","content":"I was working on a court system based on the 7 Vices and some of Dante's Inferno a long time back, but never got it completed beyond a bunch of notes. Not so much an integration of nWoD's Inferno, but taking some of the ideas in mind enough to basically change a bit of Changeling's window dressing. Still something I'd like to see mind you. The Courts of Sin, The Circles of Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T15:55:49-08:00","id":21332,"title":"","content":"I'was actually working out on this system of courts, but i'm a little bit stuck in fleshing out holydays and more of theirs philosophy.<br /> (And a better english translation, possibly.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In Kansas, the Freehold of the Yellow Smile holds the reins of a famous fast-food franchise.<br /> The courts are modeled after food, but some believe there is a hidden layer of truth - ancient pacts which have been re-modernized after these symbols.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The main difference between &quot;temporal&quot; (day / night and seasonal) freeholds and the freehold of the Yellow Smile is that the power does not pass from court to court, but it is firmly held by one, dingle court.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333233\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">On the other hand, all the changelings change periodically court - at the beginning they enroll in the freehold as Coke courtiers, then Fries courtier, then Burger. Afterwards, when the Burger courtier Breaks the oath of truthfulness (see later), they find again themselves in the Coke court.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333233\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Some courtiers prefer to remain for a longer time in the same court, but everyone is expected to change mantle, sooner or later.<br /> Even if, for someone, the &quot;later&quot; still has to come.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The court of Burger </b><br /> <b>The transubstantiated logo, The Heart Court.</b><br /> <br /> Emotion: Pride.<br /> Nickname: Ketchup-mantled , Branded Messiah , Phoenixes<br /> <br /> The courtiers of Burger feels to be the rightful Kings (terrible pun intended) of the Yellow Smile freehold. They are the essence of the brand which is made flesh, material, and coated with sauce to be glorified in their incarnation. <br /> <br /> Their philosophy is that, after the discover of their true self during their exploration as Friers, they have to reveal it with no refrain, even if it may seem terrible to themselves or others. The time of research is now finished, they have to front with courage and honesty what lies inside themselves, independently of its goodness.<br /> <br /> And, on the same time, because of their imposed sincerity, they have to drive the freehold to fabulous deeds in the mortal and faerie world: even if not leaders, they have to set the foundations for the freehold's tomorrow.<br /> <br /> All the members of the burger court have to take the oath to never lie (to others - and expecially themselves), or to be banned from the Burger court. The Oath is not codified - the precise wording is usually chosen from the applicant himself, in order to prove his capability to &quot;express&quot; himself in the world.<br /> <br /> Because of their forced sincerity, Burger courtiers are assumed as true chiefs of the freehold, and is expected form them to guide the other changelings to epic deeds in the faeric and mortal world. Burger courtesans have to set (or shift) the foundations of the Yellow smile, even in roles different from leadership, as with constructive criticism (it is known that they CAN NOT lie), planning buildings for the future, or every other long term project they feel they have to complete.<br /> <br /> Life as phoenix is stressful and hard, and many changeling voluntarily break their sincerity oath, or remain for a long time in the Fries Court in order to find the resolve necessary to become a Phoenix.<br /> <br /> Heraldry: bodily humors, visible stains, spices and strong smells, aureolas, round wafers, crowns.<br /> <br /> Concepts: grandma with no shame about intimate details of her life, valorous knight of carnal abandon, illuminate dreamer-tyrant, politician with no secret about his faults, notekeeper of truths, builder of new franchising, mystical logo designer, quirky teacher.with obscene language.<br /> <br /> Mantle: the courtiers of Burger often have subtle mantles, which reveal the metaphorical truth of the courtier itself - in particular, their vice - as if this were something glorious and sublime. Weak mantles mantle reveals as a smell or a tactile emotion, as the odor of sweat or sex, the sensation of a perfect skin, the taste of blood in the mouth. Strong mantles makes the courtier appear as a saint or a god, with fiery halos and barbecue stigmata.<br /> At the first dot of mantle, the sincerity emanated from the Ketchup-mantled is felt strongly in his words, giving him a +1 on Persuasion rolls.<br /> The third dot strengthens the force of his leadership, giving him the 9-again rule when he is the main actor of a teamwork roll.<br /> At the fifth dot, the Branded Messiah gains mystical power from his complete transparency: once per session, when indulging in his Vice in public, he refills completely his Glamour pool in addition to gain a willpower point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The court of Fries </b><br /> <br /> <b>(The Soul Oil, The Golden Court)</b><br /> <br /> Emotion: challenge.<br /> Nicknames : Krist\u00f2s, Friars, Doves<br /> <br /> As the potatoes are just pallid matter grown in the earth with no sight of the light, and then purified and fried in the fire of oil, and through this terrible ordeal, transformed in edible gold\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026so the courtiers of Fries believe that, after having abandoned what was useless through their permanence in the court of coke, now, enduring hardship, they can find their true self, their place in the world and the house they have to build to themselves. <br /> <br /> During this period, the Friers are encouraged to share experiences with others of their Court, and outside it, asking for teachings, exploring the edge, and, in general, try new things in their life. <br /> <br /> After an initial period of accustoming, they're, then, asked to step outer and outer from thir security, in order to hone their skills.<br /> <br /> (OK. HERE I NEED A LITTLE MORE FLUFF. IDEAS?) <br /> <br /> Heraldry: light, thorns, white or golden color, horizon, the dawn, tools for sculpting, friers, knifes.<br /> <br /> Concepts: Philosophic rake, scientist with attention disorder, social hedge backpacker, third-time Frier that doesn't sincerely know what to try next.<br /> <br /> Mantle: the mantle of the Friers is deep with possibility, exaltation and discovery just out a step from your comfort zone. A weak mantle may be made of whispers between a word and the other, objects may seem harder or assume a polished sheen. A high mantle is changing, and well manifest, giving the Dove a &quot;hardened&quot; appearance.<br /> At the first dot of mantle, the Friar becomes adamantine in her purpose, gaining a +1 bonus on all resolve rolls.<br /> The third dot widens the horizon of possibilities, canceling a point of penalty for the use of untrained skills (so, in general, no penalty for untrained physical or social, -2 penalty for untrained mental skills.)<br /> At the fifth dot, the Krist\u00f2s takes force from the hardships she endures - spending a point of willpower grants a +4 bonus on rolls instead than a +3.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Coke</b><br /> <b>The Fizzing Nepenthe, The Sour-Sweet Court</b><br /> <br /> Emotion: Reproach<br /> Nicknames: Bubbleheads, Past-solvers, Crows<br /> <br /> The court of Coke happily greets all the changelings coming out from the edge. The teaching of the coke Courtiers is the following - as the coke melts the food in your stomach, allowing you to take the only the essential nutrients and eliminating the waste; to decide your future, to discover your true self, you have to know your past, and only keep what is essential to you.<br /> The courtiers of Coke are encouraged to observe their fetch, try to take again posses of their past lives, greet their old friends as a new person and remembering the beautiful and horrible things of their mortal life. Those who comes back here after a permanence in the Burger Court are encouraged to think about the effects of their actions, the improvements they created for the society and the material bonds attached to themselves. And then, destroying or abandoning forever everything they do not feel anymore to be useful, so that this can not be anymore a distraction - or used agains them. <br /> <br /> Obvious to say, sometimes a Courtier makes a big mistake, and cancels or abandons something she did not really meant to, then tries to repair the damages caused by this choiche. The Court smiles quietly - it is the absence of something which weights its importance.<br /> <br /> Often, courtiers of Coke try to shepherd humans or others of their Court in this process, but never allowing themselves to take decision for them - strange dichotomy indeed, given that the killings and arsons and farewell used by the courtiers of Coke to cancel their past have often strong repercussion on others.<br /> <br /> The Murder: <br /> Once a Crow feels that she has no more useless bound to detach herself from, it is customary to gather the other Crows and announce her intention of passing on, to the Golden Court. <br /> The other members, then, come one at the time nearby and, if they think she's ready, wish her some words of advice and farewell. Otherwise, they stab her : usually it is just a touch of the edge of the blade, but it is not unheard of a person dying because of a failed attempt of &quot;Murder.&quot;<br /> At the end of the Murder, it is left to the Crow herself and to her scars to decide whether she's really ready to pass on. <br /> <br /> Symbols: trash bins, broken mirrors, closets, fires, broken chains, poppies, the color black , acid. <br /> <br /> Concept: Broker of memories, gentle divorce-specialist lawyer, Human resources manager which hires and fires her old friends, classy scrap-merchant.<br /> <br /> Mantle: the mantle of Coke is at the same time exciting and soothing, as the noise of childhood friends, flickers of black and white photos, a smell of industrial acid.<br /> Stronger mantles of Coke seems to impose themselves as a black coat around the scene, making some details shill and canceling the rest.<br /> <br /> At the first dot, the Past-Solver can take on the force of his memories: once per scene, if she has no point of willpower, she can gain one.<br /> At the third dot, her capacity to discern between important and useless things make her gain to spend, once per scene, a point of glamour in order to re-roll a perception roll. <br /> At the fifth dot, the wyrd gives back payment for everything to which the Crow renounces: once per story she can renounce to all the dots in a merit in order to take another merit with equal or lower cost.<br /> (The renounce has to be as concrete as possible: burning your Library, breaking a friendship with your Ally, giving your Resources to the poors)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T23:15:19-08:00","id":21462,"title":"","content":"That's pretty brilliant Baroqo, a Fast Food Court themed after birds and alchemy! What type of Court Contracts do you expect?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Tatterdamlion King, the 7 Sins and hell is a cool Thematic for a court! Hell themed contracts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T05:53:42-08:00","id":21576,"title":"","content":"<br /> Thanks Eldagusto, you got it!<br /> <br /> About contracts... no idea. In truth, giving the costant change, i don't even know wheter there should be a contract for each court, or a &quot;Fast-food&quot;/alchemical general contract.<br /> I'm also trying to find some alternative rule for changing courts which is not as punishing as usual (given that changing court is expected, here).<br /> But it's thought to be a png court for a road-trip game, so it's fine.<br /> <br /> I've also another court, in my closet, the &quot;Underground Court&quot;. They live in the tube of london, far away to singular muggles, but in the middle of the masses. Their ruling emotion is alienation (the tube is made to connect places and people, but crowds end up to alienate you. You're just a silent number which is expected to stay silent, on the left and not to have eye contact), and the method thanks to which they survive is a deep study of narrative and oaths, and general closeness to each other.<br /> For that court, i've contracts. (Which i posted some time ago in the other forum)<br /> <br /> Tatterdemalion, your idea is really nice - it reminds me a lot the old legend about the tithe to hell.<br /> Would you mind to share the notes? Maybe we can flesh it out a little bit more, if you like.<br /> <br /> KIng Raven, what did you thought about the Mantle and contracts of the flower courts?<br /> In particular, does the Crowned human gain any power?<br /> <br /> In the other forum there were a lot of fleshed-out alternative court systems. I remember one based on card suits... maybe we can manage to collect the alternative court systems (or their links) in one topic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:43:14-08:00","id":21711,"title":"","content":"Wow I never heard of any of these courts before, I guess I missed them! So I would be interested in your contract notes if you gots em! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:47:07-08:00","id":21714,"title":"","content":"And it would be pretty cool to have things like a Vitriol Contract for Coke, and maybe a Crucible Contract for Fries, and I don't know a Refined/Pure Contract for Burger(or maybe it would be a finished product contract?).<br /> <br /> But yeah I feel a lot of courts beyond the ones introduced in the books would have changelings expected to change courts in their life. The Courts I suggested for the Life Stages (The Ashram and the Norn Courts) would naturally have Changelings go through the courts throughout their own life journeys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:54:20-08:00","id":21805,"title":"","content":"I Pm'd you one of the two contracts. <br /> <br /> THe idea is very nice! The Phoenixes may have a Magna Opera contract (which in italian sounds really punny - Magna is a gergal expression for &quot;he eats&quot;)<br /> Otherwise, what about allowing merits (or better, tricks) (based on a terrible understanding of alchemy and fast food franchise) which need a minimum amount of mantle / goodwill?<br /> <br /> I would focus the merits on &quot;improving&quot; the natural changeling condition - so, give strange boosts to collecting glamour, incite bedlam, navigate the hedge, picking goblin fruits, oneiromancy.<br /> <br /> Example: <br /> <br /> Blend et coagula 00<br /> Requires: 4 Coke, 3 Burger<br /> <br /> As the Burger court teaches, it is possible to take a symbol, or a dream, and make it real. <br /> On the other hand, the Coke court teaches that it is possible to distill quite everything - relation, things, people in their essential meaning.<br /> Blending the two concepts, wise changeling of the Yellow Smile may take out the platonic concept of objects themselves to bring them in dreams (and vice versa).<br /> <br /> A changeling may distill the nature of a single physical object, destroying it in the process - nothing have to remain. <br /> The object has to be mundane, so tokens, goblin fruits and similar things can not be used. <br /> <br /> During dreams, the changeling may &quot;call on&quot; the object, summoning it on her side. It is possible to use such object in order to have a +2 equipment bonus on all the suitable rolls (Narrators are advised to allow &quot;wide&quot; interpretations for the use of the object. For example, a spear may be uset not only to combat, but to jump, open doors, with a flag on it to improve morale, etc...)<br /> On the other hand, a changeling may destroy the object in the dream - in this way, the physical item will appear, unmarred, at her side once she awakes.<br /> <br /> Each time you destroy the object (in the physical or dream world) roll Resolve + Occult.<br /> If you fail the roll, the item is forever lost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (this said, i think i'm threadcrapping a little and i should open an apposite thread)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T11:29:30-08:00","id":28837,"title":"","content":"For an elaborate Court, we could have a Court based on the Zodiac. An Eastern version would have the Courts change per year and a Western variety would change depending on where the sign shows up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T05:25:22-08:00","id":29847,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of a zodiac court, but 12 &quot;traditional&quot; courts (that is, with changeling divided in each one) seems to me a little bit too many. Maybe they are divided amongst the elements (fire, water, air, earth) or qualities (mobile, fix, cardinal) and each of such courts is governed by a triumvirate/quadriumvirate, each representing a sign?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T06:10:15-08:00","id":29866,"title":"","content":"Since Zodiac Courts would last so long it reminds of electing a president when deciding a Monarch as its a rulership of a Lunar year for the Chinese Zodiac.<br /> <br /> Which in turn reminds me of the idea they gave for the Donkey and Elephant court system of America, which I guess lasts 4 years for each Monarch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T06:34:07-08:00","id":29875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroqo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12917-if-we-got-a-book-introducing-new-courts-what-would-you-want?p=21576#post21576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Tatterdemalion, your idea is really nice - it reminds me a lot the old legend about the tithe to hell.<br /> Would you mind to share the notes? Maybe we can flesh it out a little bit more, if you like.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll see if I can track them down. I've had a few HDD wipes since I last tinkered with the idea, but I may have it backed up. The Tithe to Hell was definitely in mind with that; a darker undertone regarding rumored (or true) tendencies of those Courts to tithe one soul to the Gentry every appropriate time to maintain their safety or as a mortal misunderstanding that they as a whole were marked as the Tithe to Hell and in turn become Changelings if they get back out. Less &quot;The Fae give something to hell&quot; and more &quot;nope, you were marked by something you did, or who you were; you just got taken there before you died because of how interested Hell was in you.&quot; I wanted some wiggle-room where some Changelings actually believed they -did- die with enough that it could well be possible without any actual system shifts for these Courts. Its not like ghosts aren't materialized, and can't get twisted into something else via the Hedge or Arcadia... so how many of these Changelings all 6th Sense-like didn't realize they were dead until they entered &quot;limbo&quot; and &quot;hell&quot;?<br /> <br /> Last I remember I was working on a terminology shift using the Qlipoth as a start (I was wanting to intergrate other cultural elements, so it wasn't too directly related to Abrahamic faiths, but it was the initial stepping off point) right down to how they referred to Seemings and other elements, as well as a very distinct outlook on what Arcadia -really- was. Which, of course, was Hell itself to these folks. Guilt and regret complexes would play heavily as part of the trauma these Court members would be contending with.<br /> <br /> It could be a window-dressing change for a variant Changeling as a whole, or easily just the response a group that sprung up from a particular set of Gentry and regions of Arcadia who didn't really get exposure (or buy into) the meta-terms of Changeling. The Thorns, a Limbo of sorts, filled with mutilated and twisted lost souls (Hobgoblins) and wandering demons (Hobgoblins again). A lot of Dante's elements as well without a direct port over, but the City of Dis? Many of the layers of hell? Lots of ways to spin these into realms of Arcadia. Nevermind once you start using demonlogy in the context of Titles for Gentry and play around with options for one-sided Pledges and more...<br /> <br /> Something of a mish mash from various sources, as well as a bit more focus on these courts regarding the relevance of Fetches. Some spinning mortal of mythology regarding all this to fit their own experiences more so it was more two way rather than just Changelings aping mortal outlooks, art and religion alone. I wanted to get these rolling for the game I'm running right now, but it just didn't pan out time wise. I wanted to have them around to present a differing option or viewpoint on the world Changelings lived in, even alongside a more traditional Seasonal Court. Some heavy friction due to in some instances vastly differing outlooks and treatments of things, even if the mechanics underlaying it all were effectively untouched outside some general option usage from later supplements.<br /> <br /> It's still something I'd like to play around with sometime, time allowing; we have D;tD, I loved D:tF, we have Inferno and all sorts of things to use for the Infernal in nWoD, but this side-jaunt always stuck with me as having a fair bit of potential even as a set of Courts alone. I didn't want to have to use anything really outside of Changeling itself, leaving the other things optional considerations for those wanting to interconnect things more. There are some overlaps with existing courts, but, eh. That's already there with the sheer amount of material the Seasonal Courts have, so it isn't really an issue unless one makes it into one. That said; using Inferno Vestments as inspiriation (definitely not a direct port over) for the Courts of Vice/Sin Contracts? Definitely some extra mileage to be gained from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 12-14-2013, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T07:14:44-08:00","id":29889,"title":"","content":"<b>Tatterdemalion</b> What you write about the hell courts is really wonderful.<br /> <br /> Some random ideas about what the changelings may believe:<br /> <br /> <b>Fetches</b> in Dante's Divina Commedia it is said that souls are, after the Judgement (i believe), given a new phisical body. Maybe changeling believe themselves to be the souls of their own body, and Fetches their soul-less, previous self? In this case, the legend for which &quot;you can merge to your fetch&quot; would ring awesomely.<br /> <br /> <b>The tithe to hell</b> Maybe there is a &quot;pact&quot; in the freehold for which, every seven years, every court has to bring a particularly &quot;virtuous (or damned)&quot; individual to make some kind of gate of hell (i.e. a road to Arcadia) close, for other seven years. The Court which bring the most &quot;delicious&quot; gift is given some kind of boon.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghosts </b>i would put them in the mix. Obviously, darlkings are the favourite ones to deal with them.<br /> <br /> A couple of words about how i envision some of the <b>Courts</b>:<br /> <br /> - The court of wrath is more or less like summer. It focuses on honour (and revenge), martial power and war.<br /> <br /> - The court of envy focuses on the aspects of fairy magic and boons, because they want themselves to be at the same height of the <br /> <br /> - The court of sloth negates. They think that if they can &quot;disbelieve&quot; faeries, if they manage to do it hard enough.<br /> <br /> - The court of Lust tries to merge itself as deep as possible with mortal society, creating subterranean cults.<br /> <br /> - The court of Pride, on the other hand, accepts completely their faeric heritage, and tries to build a &quot;minor&quot; kingdom inside the Limbo, using Lost Souls (hobs) as slaves. <br /> <br /> - Not a lot of ideas about Gluttony and Avarice. Perhaps glamour and pacts? But it feels weak.<br /> <br /> <b>Seemings</b>: i would definitely use &quot;demonic&quot; names. Some ideas -<br /> <br /> Fairest - Luciferians, incubi/succubi, Deceivers, Princes, Presidents, Defilers, Snakes<br /> <br /> Beasts - Familiars, Devourers, Hellhounds, Cerberuses<br /> <br /> Darklings - Wraiths, Shades, Drudes, Charons, Larvae<br /> <br /> Ogres - Juggernauts, Pit-devils, Satanites, Abbadonites<br /> <br /> Elementals - ok, here i have no idea. Maybe Djinns? But it is not the same culture.<br /> <br /> Wizened - Imps, Malefactors, Fiends, Witches, Belialites, Goblins<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Eldagusto</b> i would love donkey and elephant courts!<br /> One thing which is interesting is that, beforehand, donkey and elephant were used as insults against them maybe they draw power from rage directed to them, insults, suspicion and such things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T07:27:17-08:00","id":29897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroqo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/12917-if-we-got-a-book-introducing-new-courts-what-would-you-want?p=21576#post21576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KIng Raven, what did you thought about the Mantle and contracts of the flower courts?<br /> In particular, does the Crowned human gain any power?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only done the Mantle for Violet (I have several projects on the go, and lately Hunter: Cults and Princess have been in focus) but yes, the Crown gives mortals everything they need to thrive in Freehold society: Ensorcellement, protection from The Thorns, really powerful protection from magic, social bonuses with Changelings and Pledgecraft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T09:34:08-08:00","id":30461,"title":"","content":"Boroqo I finally got the two contract messages you sent, I'll read em now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}